    "final_answer": "I have all the information needed. Let me summarize the findings.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Most downloaded machine translation model on HuggingFace focusing on English and Japanese (en-ja):**\n\n**Model: Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-en-jap**\n- **Source language:** English (en)\n- **Target language:** Japanese (jap)\n- **Pipeline:** Translation\n- **Tags:** English, jap, marian, text2text-generation\n- **Downloads last month:** 15,198\n- **OPUS readme:** en-jap\n- **Dataset:** opus\n- **Model architecture:** transformer-align\n\n### Evaluation Metrics:\n\n| Testset | BLEU | chr-F |\n|---------|------|-------|\n| bible-uedin.en.jap | 42.1 | 0.960 |\n\nThe evaluation metrics stated for this model are:\n- **BLEU score: 42.1**\n- **chr-F score: 0.960**\n\nBoth metrics were measured on the **bible-uedin.en.jap** test set.\n\nNote: This model uses the older OPUS language code \"jap\" instead of \"ja\" for Japanese, which is why it didn't appear when filtering by the standard `other=en-ja` HuggingFace filter (which only returned the tttza/fugumt-en-ja-onnx model with just 9 downloads). The Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-en-jap is the most downloaded en→ja translation model on HuggingFace.",
